  "notes": "Boot a Demolition Man ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape, step through the power-up test report (four Enters reach the main menu because the disabled claw and elevator mechanisms raise CLAW MOTOR ERROR), open the test menu, start T.1 SWITCH EDGES, then drive every switch-matrix address 11-88 and every Fliptronic address 111-118 to public 1 and back to 0, one at a time, holding each level for 1.5 s; 24 (Always Closed) and 21 (Slam Tilt) go last and 22 (Coin Door Closed) stays released. The ROM's top display line names a switch while it reads it as active, so the edge that brings a name up shows which public level the ROM treats as active, and the name is the ROM's own.",
